g roughly $13 million to Boebert's $1.2 million and holding a large cash advantage. The race has drawn wide attention, with the candidates meeting in a single televised debate covering tariffs, inflation, and January 6.\n\nThe evidence still points to Boebert. The lone public poll, from a Democratic-aligned sponsor, showed her ahead 45 to 40 in late September, and most race raters call the district Likely or Solid Republican, though a few label it a tossup. Betting markets give Laubacher roughly a one-in-four chance. A favorable midterm environment and her fundraising keep the contest competitive on paper, but the district's lean remains the dominant force.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1824, "margin": -5.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3343, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1945, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2743, "margin": -4.7}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2626, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.23, "margin": -4.7}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2582, "margin": -4.8}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2829, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2916, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2767, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3037, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.311, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.297, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2522, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2256, "margin": -4.7}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2601, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.2778, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2282, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.1951, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.2266, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.276, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.2137, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.2086, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "202